{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>To Him who rides</b> — connected with the yod, after the manner of the beast upon which I ride. And the meaning: the name of the heavens." "And the meaning of <b>קדם</b> — it has a sod, corresponding to the children of the generation, and פעול יתן קול עוז."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 68, :notes {0 "The argument is cryptic; translated hyper-literally. The phrase 'שמי השמים' may refer to a divine name associated with the heavens, but the syntax is compressed and no expansion is supplied per discipline."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:33:21.774286641Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}